hi Marc,
 My first thought on this is that because the Bayes estimator should be consistent with the posterior MODE, and the model having so many parameters, it's probably just the case that the posterior mean in 12 dimensions just isn't so close to the posterior mode.

 I think you could test this theory out in a vague sort of way by simulating a huge data set (1000 sites?) under the same model and then see if the posterior means are quite a bit closer....

On Mon, Feb 23, 2015 at 8:41 AM, Kery Marc <marc...@vogelwarte.ch> wrote:

> Dear all,
>
>
