Dear Andy,

your guess was quite correct. For very large sample sizes (I simulated 4500 sites), the MLEs and the Bayesian estimator correspond much better, see here below. So what does that mean ? That with small sample sizes the posteriors may be more skewed and therefore the mean matches the mode (and therefore the MLE) less well ?

Kind regards  --- Marc

