It is interesting that the Bayesian estimates almost always have larger uncertainty, which might speak to the shape of the posteriors (maybe longer chains would make a difference).

I'm sure things would fare better with some model averaging for each approach, under the lower sample sizes.  Only useful for comparing predictions, but you could see how they match up with predictions from the data generation.

